        <div class="step-arrow" id="a-pm6">&#9660;</div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-body" id="b-pm6">
        <div class="res-list">
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"></path><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name">"Algebra" by Michael Artin</div>
              <div class="res-desc">The best undergraduate algebra textbook. Artin is concrete where many algebra books are abstract — he motivates groups through symmetry, rings through polynomials, and fields through number systems. Covers: groups, subgroups, homomorphisms, quotient groups, rings, ideals, fields, Galois theory. More geometric and intuitive than Dummit & Foote. The exercises range from computational to deeply theoretical.</div>
