            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"></path><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name">"Algebra" by Serge Lang</div>
              <div class="res-desc">The graduate-level reference. Lang covers everything: groups, rings, modules, fields, Galois theory, homological algebra, commutative algebra, representation theory. Dense and comprehensive. Use as your reference encyclopedia after learning from Artin. When you need to look up a theorem or definition at the graduate level, Lang is where you go.</div>
