        <div class="step-arrow" id="a-pm7">&#9660;</div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-body" id="b-pm7">
        <div class="res-list">
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"></path><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name">"Topology" by James Munkres</div>
              <div class="res-desc">The definitive undergraduate topology textbook, used by virtually every mathematics department in the world. Part I (general topology): topological spaces, connectedness, compactness, countability, separation axioms, metrization. Part II (algebraic topology): fundamental group, covering spaces, Seifert-van Kampen theorem. Munkres writes with exceptional clarity. Every theorem is motivated, every proof is clean. Do every exercise in Chapters 1-7 at minimum.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag must">The standard</span><span class="rtag book">Textbook</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><polygon points="10 8 16 12 10 16 10 8"></polygon></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLLq_gUfXAnkl8bjQh-hGQ9u24xZP9x0dx" target="_blank" class="res-link">Topology & Geometry by Dr. Tadashi Tokieda (YouTube) <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">Tokieda is one of the most engaging mathematics lecturers alive. His topology lectures use physical intuition and toy demonstrations to make abstract concepts visceral. Watch before tackling each Munkres chapter for motivation and intuition.</div>
