            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><polygon points="10 8 16 12 10 16 10 8"></polygon></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLZHQObOWTQDMXMi3bUMThGdYqos36X_lA" target="_blank" class="res-link">3Blue1Brown — Topology-related videos <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">Videos on the Borsuk-Ulam theorem, surface topology, and related concepts. Perfect visual introductions before formal study. 3B1B's video on topology showing why you can always find two antipodal points with the same temperature is a masterpiece of mathematical storytelling.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag vid">YouTube</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="insight"><b>Where topology appears in other domains:</b> Topological Data Analysis (TDA) is a growing field in ML that uses persistent homology to find shape in high-dimensional data. In physics, topological quantum computing is a leading approach to fault-tolerant quantum computers. In robotics, configuration spaces are topological objects. Topology is not abstract luxury — it is increasingly applied infrastructure.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

