      <div class="step-body" id="b-pm8">
        <div class="res-list">
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"></path><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name">"An Introduction to the Theory of Numbers" by Hardy & Wright</div>
              <div class="res-desc">The classic number theory text, still unmatched for elegance. Covers divisibility, primes, congruences, quadratic residues, continued fractions, and Diophantine approximation. Number theory is essential for cryptography (RSA, elliptic curves) and has deep connections to algebra and analysis. Hardy's writing is a masterclass in mathematical exposition.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag must">Classic</span><span class="rtag book">Textbook</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"></path><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name">"Differential Geometry of Curves and Surfaces" by Manfredo do Carmo</div>
              <div class="res-desc">The standard introduction to differential geometry. Covers curves, surfaces, Gauss map, intrinsic geometry, Gauss-Bonnet theorem. This is the mathematics of curved spaces — essential for general relativity, computer graphics, and robotics. do Carmo's exposition is geometric and intuitive before becoming rigorous.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag must">For physics + robotics</span><span class="rtag book">Textbook</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"></path><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name">"Complex Analysis" by Lars Ahlfors</div>
              <div class="res-desc">The standard graduate complex analysis text. Covers analytic functions, complex integration, Cauchy's theorem, residues, conformal mapping, analytic continuation. Complex analysis is the most beautiful branch of mathematics — theorems here are more powerful and surprising than anywhere else. Essential for quantum mechanics, signal processing, and advanced physics.</div>
