            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-950-differential-geometry-fall-2008/" target="_blank" class="res-link">MIT 18.950 — Differential Geometry (OCW) <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">Free MIT course with lecture notes. Covers classical differential geometry of curves and surfaces. Excellent companion to do Carmo.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag vid">MIT OCW</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="do-box"><b>Study order suggestion:</b> Complex analysis and number theory can be studied in parallel with each other after real analysis and algebra. Differential geometry requires multivariable calculus and linear algebra. If your primary interest is physics, prioritize differential geometry. If CS/cryptography, prioritize number theory. If ML theory, prioritize complex analysis (for characteristic functions and Fourier analysis).</div>
