            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name">"Introductory Functional Analysis with Applications" by Erwin Kreyszig</div>
              <div class="res-desc">The gentlest introduction to functional analysis — Banach spaces, Hilbert spaces, bounded linear operators, spectral theory. Kreyszig motivates every definition with applications. This is the mathematics of infinite-dimensional vector spaces, which is the language of quantum mechanics, PDEs, and modern optimization theory. Prerequisite: real analysis (Rudin) and linear algebra.</div>
