            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"></path><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name">"Category Theory in Context" by Emily Riehl (free PDF)</div>
              <div class="res-desc">Free at math.jhu.edu/~eriehl/context.pdf. Category theory is "the mathematics of mathematics" — it studies the structure that all mathematical structures share. Categories, functors, natural transformations, adjunctions, limits, Yoneda lemma. Riehl is the best modern expositor. This connects to: type theory in CS, database schema design, functional programming (monads, functors), and theoretical physics. Prerequisite: abstract algebra and topology.</div>
