        <div class="insight"><b>The polymath payoff of category theory:</b> Category theory is the ultimate cross-domain language. It formalizes the idea of "structural similarity" between different mathematical (and scientific) domains. A functor between categories IS the formal version of an analogy. Learning category theory literally trains you to see the deep structural connections between fields — the exact skill that defines a polymath.</div>
