        <div class="step-arrow" id="a-pm11">&#9660;</div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-body" id="b-pm11">
        <div class="res-list">
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"></path><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name">"Introduction to Electrodynamics" by David J. Griffiths</div>
              <div class="res-desc">Universally regarded as the best undergraduate E&M textbook ever written. Griffiths has a gift for making vector calculus feel natural. Covers: electrostatics, magnetostatics, electrodynamics, Maxwell's equations, electromagnetic waves, radiation, relativistic electrodynamics. Every problem is worth solving — Griffiths problems are famous for being challenging but fair, and they build physical intuition that no amount of lecture-watching can replace.</div>
