              <div class="res-desc">Design a novel cryptographic protocol, implement it, and formally verify its security properties using Coq or Lean. Requires: number theory (algebra over finite fields), CS theory (computational complexity of breaking the protocol), software engineering (implementation), and formal methods (machine-checked proofs of correctness). Domains touched: 4.</div>
